_at":"2026-04-02T16:36:40Z","updated_at":"2026-04-08T14:37:03Z","closed_at":"2026-04-08T14:35:10Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in: v4.6.2.stable.arch_linux [001aa128b], v4.7.dev3.official [60fff00a6], v4.5.2.stable.official [6ce3de25a]\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.6.2.stable (001aa128b) - Arch Linux #1 SMP PREEMPT_DYNAMIC Thu, 26 Mar 2026 19:20:28 +0000 on Wayland - X11 display driver, Multi-window, 1 monitor - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3060 (nvidia; 595.58.03) - AMD Ryzen 5 2600 Six-Core Processor (12 threads) - 31.28 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen enabling that warning should be treated as errors, the warning errors appear below actual errors.\n\nMy thinking is that, if I want warnings to be treated as errors, then they should be treated as errors and appear in order on the error list.\n\nNow I'm looking at line 2 and look at the first error in the list (because it's the first error by line number, so I look at the first error in the list) and I'm confused as to why it says the error is about Vector2 even though there isn't one at line 2. It gets more confusing with more complex scripts.\n\n<img width=\"1142\" height=\"322\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/16cfad9d-e4b7-4ecb-9633-7fc33518149b\" />\n\nIf this is desired for any reason, please enlighten me, because I can't think of any reason.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Create new project and script\n2. Add this code\n```gdscript\nfunc _foo() -> void:\n\tvar _i: int = 1.0\n\nfunc _bar() -> void:\n\tvar _v: Vector2 = 3\n```\n3. Observe errors\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id